1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,267
Great events move together.

2
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:08,000
Meet CrewLift: every change, a stronger plan.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,900
This demonstration follows Makers Morning, a fictional community event with eight volunteers and three one-hour
shifts.

4
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:22,000
CrewLift connects a changing schedule to clear personal next steps.

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:31,533
Here's today's update: Ava is away, the creative workshop needs a second facilitator, and Chloe stays on the
opening gallery tour.

6
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:39,000
We give CrewLift the update in everyday language.

7
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:48,200
NVIDIA Nemotron, running through Nebius Token Factory, turns that update into structured planning rules with
supporting source passages.

8
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,533
CrewLift validates the rules, then computes the recovery options.

9
00:00:52,533 --> 00:01:00,000
The coordinator can inspect every extracted constraint.

10
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,100
Keep the rhythm focuses updates on the smallest possible affected crew.

11
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,233
Share the energy spreads assignments more evenly.

12
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:17,000
Both plans fill all ten required places, giving the coordinator two clear ways forward.

13
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,267
Let's choose Keep the rhythm.

14
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:26,867
Ten places covered. Seven original assignments retained. Three people to update, with clear next steps.

15
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:36,000
An independent exhaustive check confirms that three is the minimum for full coverage in this scenario.

16
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,900
The roster brings the result into view.

17
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:42,500
Every assignment connects a teammate to a role and a time.

18
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:50,000
Personal change cards give each affected volunteer a clear next move.

19
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:54,533
Accept the plan, and it becomes the team's new starting point.

20
00:01:54,533 --> 00:02:01,267
The action pack brings together a roster spreadsheet, a structured plan, and a readable handoff brief.

21
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:09,000
A complete, versioned plan is ready for the next huddle.

22
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,667
The run details connect the NVIDIA model call to the plan you see.

23
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:22,000
Inspect the model identity, token usage, and input and output fingerprints behind this run.

24
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,600
Exact optimization and a separate constraint audit work together.

25
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:35,000
We verified ninety-five independent solver cases, twenty-four development tests, and ten workflow groups.

26
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:39,367
CrewLift connects a changing schedule to a coordinated team.

27
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:42,000
Every change. A stronger plan.
